# Requirements. 

- Git commit with descriptive comments every time you make major changes to the scripts or codebase. 
- Every time you resolve a new (technically interesting) error, add a note at the top of the [logs.md file](./.cursor/notes/log.md). Conventions: 
    - New entries at the TOP of file. 
    - Markdown section header (`#`) should be today's date. 
    - Always put the git commit hash on the error report so we know what version of the codebase exhibited said behavior. 
    - Be as detailed as possible  


# Forbidden things and what you should do instead. 

- NEVER use `rm` to delete files. Always use `rip` (safe deletion) instead. 
